--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Derived work: SO-ARM100
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The UJ201 arm is a derivative of the Standard Open SO-100 / SO-101 Arms by
TheRobotStudio, used under the Apache License 2.0.

    https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100

THE MECHANICAL DESIGN HAS BEEN MODIFIED. UJ201 is not the SO-100 or SO-101 and
should not be taken as representing them. It is heavily reworked: a two-axis
universal-joint shoulder in place of the original shoulder arrangement, a
redesigned forearm, wrist and end effector, and additional structural parts
(base binder strip, cradle, roof, U-bridge). Some upstream geometry survives;
much does not. Faults in this design are ours, not TheRobotStudio's.

This applies to the CAD under cad/, the per-link meshes under meshes/, and the
URDF description under urdf/, all of which trace back to that design.

The upstream repository asks to be cited (CITATION.cff):

    Standard Open SO-100 & SO-101 Arms
    Rob Knight, Pepijn Kooijmans, Remi Cadene, Simon Alibert, Michel Aractingi,
    Dana Aubakirova, Adil Zouitine, Russi Martino, Steven Palma,
    Caroline Pascal, Thomas Wolf
    2024. https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100

Please carry that citation forward if you use this arm.

